{"seq":1,"mint":"C4","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"the key is `fs::canonicalize`d (absolute by construction)","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F6","F18","F21"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"/// Resolve `path` to the key used for overlap matching: its canonical\n/// absolute form when that succeeds, the path as given otherwise.\n/// Canonicalization can fail on some platforms/filesystems even for a\n/// path that exists (e.g. a permissions issue on an ancestor\n/// directory); falling back keeps this infallible rather than losing\n/// the observation over it.\nfn resolve_key(path: &Path) -> String {\n    fs::canonicalize(path).map(|p| p.display().to_string()).unwrap_or_else(|_| path.display().to_string())\n}","why":"The key falls back to the path as given when canonicalization fails, so it is not absolute by construction.","quoted":true}],"at":1790111710,"cost":0.0037804440000000004,"elapsed_ms":12095,"attempts":4,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":1,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":1}
